}
By default, OpenSearch wraps the matching string in <em> tags, provides up to 100 characters of
context around the match, and breaks content into sentences by identifying punctuation marks,
spaces, tabs, and line breaks. All of these settings are customizable:
POST https://search-my-domain.us-west-1.es.amazonaws.com/movies/_search
{
"size": 20,
"query": {
"multi_match": {
"query": "house",
"fields": ["title^4", "plot^2", "actors", "directors"]
}
},
"highlight": {
"fields": {
"plot": {}
},
"pre_tags": "<strong>",
"post_tags": "</strong>",
"fragment_size": 200,
"boundary_chars": ".,!? "
}
}
